Date: 2026-09-08. Author: `/root/round211_rational_scout`.
Status: `NO_FRESH_SLATE`; author desk, not independent manuscript review.

## Outcome and counting boundary

This bounded pass supplies **zero fresh literal nominations, zero retained
candidates, zero scientific executions, and zero new closed-attempt
increments**. The capacity was at most three fresh nominations, not a quota.
The table below contains already-defined constructions and primitive-level
exclusions, not three new attempts. No paper number or pilot contract was
requested, allocated, or executed.

The project research skill's early-rejection and primitive-subtraction gates
caused this closure. `research-lit` supplied primary-source/read-boundary
discipline; `proof-writer` supplied the explicit assumptions for the small
background obstructions in [PROOF_PACKAGE.md](PROOF_PACKAGE.md). Those
obstructions receive no new-science credit. There is no claim that all planar
matching dynamics have been exhausted or that every possible variant is old.

Only this new lane was written. Older evidence, the checkpoint preparation,
central controls, Git, manuscripts, reviews and external release were untouched.

## Actual constructions screened before nomination

| Existing construction / entrance | Exact rule or mechanism read | Why no fresh nomination follows |
|---|---|---|
| Crossing-component section and ordered local uncrossing | P130 replaces each crossing component, on sorted endpoint support, by consecutive pairs. Old M01 resolves the lexicographically least crossing `(a,c),(b,d)`, `a<b<c<d`, into `(a,d),(b,c)`. | P130's component/support section is an old retraction with an old target-wise sibling/decorated inverse. M01 already records the exact crossing clock, opener-preserving stack endpoint and graded terminal basins; its sorting primitive was already subtracted. Neither literal is nominated again. |
| Dyck reassociation / Motzkin summit erosion / Tamari Pop | P144 fixes a primitive path and sends `C1 C2 ... Ck`, `C1=U A D`, to `U A C2 D C3 ... Ck` otherwise. The old ledger explicitly contains parallel `U H^r D -> H^(r+2)` flattening. Hong's author abstract defines Tamari Pop as the meet of a state and its lower covers. | P144 already contains the factor-count clock and terminal inverse for its literal selector. Summit flattening is an explicit old exclusion. Hong establishes an existing named dynamics, not a blank new rule. No scheduler change, reflection, path/tree encoding, or unproved inverse is promoted here. |
| Regular-star diagram folding and reversible relabelling | In a regular-star semigroup, `F(x)=x x*` is a projection-valued retraction and `J(x)=x*` is an involution. Fixed endpoint relabellings, when actually bijective on the state space, are permutations. | Their temporal behavior follows directly from the stated algebraic identities or bijectivity. They do not supply a fresh nontrivial temporal axis. This says nothing about arbitrary fixed multiplication, `x -> x^2`, or all-target root enumeration. |

The exact old literals above are recorded only to resolve collisions. No new
rule on planar matchings was instantiated and tested. In particular, a source
on an uncrossing partial order does not by itself own every deterministic
selector of its covers, and an idempotent classification does not by itself
solve dynamics of arbitrary diagram powers.

## Historical originals actually used

Six original files are pinned in
[HISTORICAL_INPUT_PINS.sha256](HISTORICAL_INPUT_PINS.sha256); paths there are
workspace-relative. Two are PDFs, four are textual originals. All six hashes
were obtained before and after the collection by native `sha256sum`, and
the two raw outputs were compared by an actual native `cmp -s` (exit 0).
This establishes unchanged bytes over this collection, not a replay of old
mathematics. No old verifier or old build was invoked.

1. `papers/130-crossing-component-fibre-geometry/main.tex`: lines 1–310 read,
   including the literal section, retraction proof and all four steps of
   the sibling inverse. The largest-fibre theorem statement was seen; its
   later proof was not re-audited. The actual `main.pdf` first three pages
   were separately extracted and read, not visually re-reviewed.
2. `papers/144-leftmost-dyck-reassociation/main.tex`: lines 1–270 and 285–353
   read, including the literal selector, theorem statement, closed-orbit
   proof and the layer calculation. The later terminal-fibre proof was not
   re-audited. Its theorem statement and explicit inverse are already enough
   to prevent treating the same literal as fresh. The actual `main.pdf`
   first three pages were separately extracted and read.
3. `docs/papers147_151_sequence/scouting/combinatorial/SCOUT.md`: lines
   44–177 read; the complete M01 section supplies the exact update and its
   old mechanism/subtraction boundary. This is not an independent replay of
   the historical numerical profile.
4. `docs/papers197_201_sequence/scouting/word_poset_lane/BREADTH_AND_KILL_LEDGER.md`:
   the pre-denominator collision table (captured lines 65–88) explicitly
