## Primary sources and exact reading limits

| Primary source | What was actually read | Scope of use |
|---|---|---|
| Igor Dolinka, James East, Athanasios Evangelou, Des FitzGerald, Nicholas Ham, James Hyde, Nicholas Loughlin and James D. Mitchell, *Enumeration of idempotents in planar diagram monoids*, [author HTML](https://arxiv.org/html/1507.04838), Journal of Algebra 522 (2019), 351–385, [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2018.11.014) | Browser body lines 0–209, particularly regular-star definition at 71, Lemma 2.1 at 76–105, Lemma 2.3 and its proof, and Jones/Motzkin regular-star statement at 186. | The regular-star hypotheses and projection identity support the elementary folding obstruction. Later classification/enumeration proofs and all-power inverse dynamics were not read or imported. |
| Letong Hong, *The Pop-stack-sorting Operator on Tamari Lattices*, Advances in Applied Mathematics 139 (2022), 102362, [author abstract](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.10030), [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2022.102362) | Author metadata and abstract only. It explicitly defines Pop and reports the sortable-depth generating function and image count. HTML body was 404; publisher body was 403. | Existing literal definition and abstract-level research pointer only. No proof or target-wise fibre formula is attributed to an unread body. |
| Thomas Lam, *The uncrossing partial order on matchings is Eulerian*, [author abstract](https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.5671), submitted 22 June 2014 | Author metadata and abstract only; HTML body was 404. | Confirms the named resolving-crossings poset as a prior topic. Does not prove ownership of a deterministic selector or any exact selected clock. |

The rendered diagram-monoid body displays an August 24, 2026 date, while the
known journal item is 2019; it is not labelled a new 2026 publication here.
Only primary sources are premises. Search snippets from secondary sites are
preserved as returned but do not establish theorem claims. No new arXiv PDF
was downloaded: the literature skill's default `ARXIV_DOWNLOAD=false`
remained in force. Optional Zotero/Obsidian clients were unavailable; the
arXiv fetch helper was not found, so the skill's web fallback was used.

